e understands that won't happen  but what else do you do when someone you  love is being taken away towards a  horrible fate it seems like most fans  have turned against margot and want to  see her get what she has coming but i  still find her sympathetic and the  performances here really made this scene  hit hard for me in another difficult  situation first gentleman larry is being  interviewed in a house subcommittee  hearing on nasa contracts the  implication is that he's using his  influence to hand out contracts to  private firms that he favors and he  seems to be doing a pretty good job of  defending himself right up until things  turn to questions about an affair this  was set up at the end of the last  episode and we see him bring in the aid  in question to ask who he's been talking  to given the power dynamics in play it's  pretty brutal to watch this aide realize  what's going to happen to his life as a  result but it works to show us the lanes  larry might go to to try to fight  against these totally true accusations  understandably ellen tears into him when  she finds out she wants to know why he  couldn't keep it in his pants for even  one term and what's so special about  this aid that he would jeopardize  everything they worked for they have an  intense exchange where larry pleads his  case that all ends up being overshadowed  when he mentions pam's name when they're  talking about making sacrifices because  ellen believed her cover story when she  left she was under the impression that  pam left her to go back to her partner  she's shocked to find out that she  really left so that ellen can move  forward with her career she also feels  betrayed that larry didn't tell her the  truth and that makes you wonder what  will happen when news of his affair  starts getting out they bring in a karl  rove type who's telling a story about  lee atwater on his way in just to remind  you how nasty this politics business is  and he suggests they need to go after  the person who brought the questions up  because he's already had a sex scandal  and he believes that he has more  skeletons in his closet there's a moment  when he says their best defense is their  picture-perfect marriage and even though  ellen and larry know this is all an  elaborate lie they also understand that  he's right apparently it doesn't sit  right with ellen though and after she  leaves we see her clear her schedule to  make a low-key trip to see pam she  arrives at her front door and asks to  come in but we'll have to wait until  next week to see what happens when they  talk  i mentioned before that i wasn't really  sure about this jimmy storyline and it  picks back up in this episode where we  see he's living at danny's place with  his wife and later we'll see her tell  her husband in a call that she's worried  about him part of that is his new  friends which i don't know what to call  them maybe nasa and on or something like  that and we see that they're trying to  use his connections for something they  have planned it seems like he's set up  to fall for the attention that they give  him and it doesn't seem likely that it's  sincere sonny goes with him to jsc to  try to get a hold of a badge and the  whole thing makes you feel bad for  what's happening it's clear she's trying  to make him complicit and he's running  into all of these people who know his  parents and are happy to see him in the  end he grabs rossi's badge after he  shows him this great tribute to his mom  and that first letter she got during  training that changed her life and it  all just kind of makes you feel dirty  rossi's the guy who gave tracy another  chance at jamestown when she was really  messing up and giving him a lot of  problems so the history there it's all  just uh  later at home all of this makes jimmy  feel some remorse and he decides to call  sonny and try to talk her into taking  the badge back he finds out that they've  already used it when they show up at his  house with the statues of his parents  initially he seems relieved and almost  thinks it's funny but it makes you  wonder if there's more to the plan that  he doesn't know about having this in his  possession could implicate him in  something much worse and i think there's  a good chance they're setting him up on  mars the team that did the right thing  and went and saved the soviets and then  got there first are looking pretty  bummed out the astronauts at happy  valley base are dealing with the fallout  from will's announcement and being left  out of this secret mission on the bright  side at least they have a lot more room  to work with and it looks like they may  have fixed some of the problems because  they're not all sitting around sweating  kelly has a call with alexei who tips  her off that they're getting ready to  start drilling she gets upset because  she hasn't finished her tests on the  core sample and she talks to ed to try  to get him to wait until she's done with  her work he just shrugs it off saying  they've done everything they're required  to do and stresses the fact that nasa is  the one who came up with these rules  over at helios base danny is continuing  to pop pills and it's starting to become  clear that there's something wrong with  him ed has to call his name several  times in front of the group during a  meeting while he is just sort of staring  at lights blinking on the wall when he  walks into him spacing out after a call  with his wife he gives a look to show  that he knows there's something going on  but he doesn't do anything about it a  little later just to really drive the  point home danny flips out and stomps a  robotic toy dog to death in front of  everyone and while this was a little bit  goofy it's a great choice to show how  unhinged he is of course this thing is  annoying him but come on it looks like  an adorable puppy this earns him a  talking to from ed where he takes him  off the flight to the drilling site he  also calls him out for taking drugs but  still doesn't go any further he just  assigns him to help out nick on  communication and then danny acts up and  looks like he wants to hit him and  instead of confining him to quarters or  sending him back to polaris ed just  punks him out and leaves it at that  back on earth elena meets with her  husband and we learn that they're  separated the implication is that over  the last couple of years that we skipped  ahead those problems we heard them  discussing about her always being at  work and everything else with her father  finally caught up to them as part of her  investigation she asked him to help her  look at the list of people who had  access to the plans that the soviets got  their hands on after we get the  impression that elena is hoping that  they might be able to get back together  and that her father's situation is  getting worse her husband brings up that  it might not be someone that works for  her implying that it could be someone  above her that is compromised later she  goes into margot's office and it seems  like she's going to accuse her but  instead she thinks it's her assistant  emma margot laughs this off because it's  actually pretty funny but the reality is  that elena went there because she hasn't  been able to believe that margot could  be the one who's working with the  soviets and as someone who hasn't  completely turned my back on margot this  is truly horrifying watching her  gaslight elena and get to the point of  threatening her i mean i know her career  is on the line and it's the logical path  for her to take but there's no excusing  it if the shoe were on the other foot  she'd be doing the exact same thing  elena is and so when we see her go out  into the lobby and finally have the  realization as she's looking at margot's  picture there's a satisfaction but it's  all just tragic the drilling operation  is on the way and out on the ridge the  soviet commander asked the question i  wonder what this valley will look like  in 10 20 or 100 years and he probably  should have thought more in the scale of  20 minutes but we'll get to that they  start drilling and they get ready for  his part back at the hab danny decides  to prep with a handful of pills they're  monitoring the pressure to make sure  that the drilling site doesn't explode  and nick steps away to run some numbers  leaving danny in charge i'm not sure if  it's implied that he's so wasted that he  can't respond or that he's doing it on  purpose to sabotage ed he's definitely  wasted but he also has some flashes of  the confrontation with that but it  doesn't really matter because he doesn't  do his job and things turn catastrophic  it's chaotic and i'm not sure what the  damage will be when the dust settles but  ed and isabel are injured from the drill  in the beginning they bring them back in  the msam and then all hell breaks loose  when the ridge starts to come down danny  is able to get ed to safety and it  looked like the soviet commander who  went ahead to prepare the med bay made  it into the other half beyond that  alexei luiza nick and isabel seem to get  caught in the dust if not the rock slide  that's rolling over the base  at the very least the msam will probably  be lost and it's possible that kelly's  boyfriend and the only person who knew  what danny did to cause the accident  will be somewhere on the scale of  injured to dead and the episode ends  there  so this episode had a really thrilling  ending and the tension is being  ratcheted up across the board i still  haven't really warmed up to the jimmy  storyline and while it was overall a  good episode i think what knocks it down  a little bit for me is that the  characters that i like are making bad  decisions and none of them feel like  they're going to be able to get out  clean you can understand why they're  doing the things they're doing but  they're frustrating ed letting danny  slide so much how can you defend his  decision to put the crew member he knows  is high anywhere near the drilling  operation he's got such a blind spot and  lives may be lost as a result i guess  this is why margot didn't want to test  pilot to be the commander of the mars  mission but i'm hoping to see ed turn  things around because trying to treat  dany like gordo is not the right way to  go i guess things are moving along in  that story and that's a good thing but  if nick dies then no one would know that  he's responsible and where do we go from  there i know margot's been focused on  getting sergey and his family out but  for as smart and in control as she is i  hope she has a better plan than throwing  elena under the bus to save her own skin  it's possible there's no coming back for  her and this downfall will serve a  latest story since she's the one that  would probably be in charge next season  but geez there's a lot hanging over  these two right now and you would kind  of hate to see margot go out like that  there were a couple of character scenes  that stood out margot putting up her  guard emotionally as sergey was saying  goodbye wren schmidt really nailed that  scene i also liked the handheld shots of  the board with tracy's picture when  jimmy was looking at it they haven't  really developed his character much so  it seems smart to lean on him losing his  parents in those scenes since we do have  feelings about them i guess what's most  interesting is that everything sorta  ended on cliffhanger so the next episode  should be a massive one after this crazy  ending i can't wait to see where things  go and i think that's a good place to  leave things let me know in the comments  what you think will happen next and what  you thought about this episode please  like this video if you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already and thanks for watching i'll  talk to you soon

